melody:
# Chorus (the original is in cut time; written here with quarter-note beats)
"Toot, toot, Toot-sie, goo'-bye!
r Eb5 C5(2) Eb5 C5(2) Eb5 C5(4) ~C5(4)
Toot, toot, Toot-sie, don't cry.
r Bb4 G4(2) Bb4 G4(2) Bb4 F4(4) ~F4 r r(2)
The choo-choo train that takes me
r D4 Eb4 G4 Bb4(2) Bb4(2) Bb4(4) D4(4)
a-way from you, no words can tell how sad it makes me.
r D4 F4 Ab4 C5(2) C5(2) C5 Bb4 D5 A4 C5 Bb4 C5 D5
Kiss me, Toot-sie, and then
r Eb5 C5(2) Eb5 C5(2) Eb5 C5(4) ~C5(4)
do it o-ver a-gain.
r Bb4 G4(2) Bb4 G4(2) Bb4 F4(4) ~F4 r r(2)
Watch for the mail, I'll nev-er fail.
Eb5 D5 Db5 C5 ~C5(2) r(2) Eb5 D5 Db5 C5 ~C5(2) r
If you don't get a let-ter then you'll know I'm in jail.
Eb4 Bb4 A4 Ab4 G4 Bb4 A4 Ab4 G4 Bb4 A4 Ab4 G4 ~G4 r r(2)
Tut, tut, Toot-sie, don't cry!
r Eb5 C5(2) Eb5 C5(2) Eb5 C5(4) ~C5(4)
Toot, toot, Toot-sie, goo'-bye!"
r Bb4 G4(2) Bb4 G4(2) Bb4 Eb5(3) r r(4)

